(PRC-33 — `Execute "<path>".` performs execve(2) and replaces the current
 process image entirely: the line after it never runs.
 SAFETY: the target is /bin/sh with a fixed, harmless -c script. A leaf
 must do the same — an allowlisted binary and a fixed argument list, never
 a generated command line (plan 323 Tier CONFINE).
